## Deck

::bg{location="deck" time="dusk"}
::music{playback="start" mood="sad" volume="down"}
@narrator{code="0010"}: Seawater leaves Ilo's lungs in one long, burning heave.
::actor{character="brann" anchor="left" action="fadeInUp"}
@brann{code="0010" emotion="grim"}: Breathe, boy. You were down there four minutes. Nobody comes back from four minutes.
@ilo{code="0010"}: The crown. I saw the crown on the throne.
@brann{code="0020"}: Everyone who goes down sees the crown. Most of them stay with it.
::actor{character="sefa" anchor="right" action="fadeInUp"}
@sefa{code="0010" emotion="surprised"}: He's warm, Brann. He's warm. The sea gave him back.
@brann{code="0030" emotion="grim"}: Then the sea wants something from him. Get him dry, and get him fed.
@narrator{code="0020"}: Somewhere below the keel, something very large turns over in its sleep.
